  "title": "A crowded day in the model catalog",
  "summary": "New text, image, video, and realtime audio options arrived alongside sharper model discovery and a sturdier path for generation retries.\n\nMuse Glimmer 30B and Qwen3.8 2.4T A95B joined the text lineup. Gemini moved to 3.7 Flash, Muse Spark to 1.2, Grok to 4.6, and DeepSeek Pro to its 0813 checkpoint. A community contribution also made GPT-5 reasoning summaries available through Azure Responses when callers set a supported reasoning effort.\n\nSeedance 2.0 Mini and Fast, MiniMax H3 video, and Grok Imagine Image 2.0 added creative choices. Scribe realtime transcription now uses the OpenAI-compatible WebSocket protocol. Speech work brought ElevenLabs dialogue into `/v1/audio/speech`, made Qwen TTS use `instructions`, and expanded the simple audio URL to support every speech model.\n\nA community contribution added favorites and persistent filters to Model Monitor. Model discovery endpoints gained a `community` filter, while community model owners gained optional per-user request limits and a confirmation step for activation changes. API-key permissions were aligned with canonical model IDs; new publishable keys now have zero direct-spend budget and cannot be created with a non-zero one. The keys dashboard also gives owners clearer status information.",
  "pr_count": 38,
